  <content>
  <section>
    <section class="check-understanding">
      <exercise data-content-id="8e0f0500-55dd-4440-9978-28a0af0a9367">
        <problem>
          <para>
      <para>For questions 1 – 4, use the following:</para>
      <para>Function \(h\) describes the height of a ball, in inches, after \(n\)<emphasis> </emphasis>bounces and is defined
        by the equation \(h(n)=120 \cdot (\frac{4}{5})^n\).</para>
      <para> What is \(h(3)\)? Round to the nearest integer. Think about what it represents in this situation.</para>
      </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>61</para>
          <para>
      <para>The correct answer is 61. After 3 bounces, the bounce height is about 61 inches. </para>
    </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </section>
